{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he lifted his eyes.</b> He directed himself to look." "<b>Standing over him.</b> Facing him, as though waiting to speak with him once he was free from the awesome vision — for those waiting by a person to speak with him are called נִצָּבִים עָלָיו, as in לְהִתְאַפֵּק לְכָל הַנִּצָּבִים עָלָיו (Genesis 45:1), and similarly וְכָל הָעָם נִצָּב עָלֶיךָ (Exodus 18:14)." "<b>And he ran toward them.</b> Before they drew near to speak with him." "<b>From the entrance of the tent.</b> He began from the entrance to run in their honor — for alacrity toward a thing indicates its importance in the eyes of the one who hastens toward it, as in וַיְמַהֵר מֹשֶׁה וַיִּקֹּד אַרְצָה וַיִּשְׁתַּחוּ (Exodus 34:8)." "<b>And bowed to the ground.</b> For their appearance was awesome, as it says: וּמַרְאֵהוּ כְּמַרְאֵה מַלְאַךְ הָאֱלֹהִים נוֹרָא מְאֹד (Judges 13:6) — and he supposed them to be emissaries of some king."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:32.743250244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}